    "why_memoization_improves": "Memoization optimizes the algorithm by storing the results of previously computed Fibonacci numbers. When the function encounters a previously calculated number, it retrieves the result from the memoization table (dictionary `memo`) instead of recalculating it. This avoids redundant computations, significantly reducing the execution time, especially for larger values of n."
  },
